Essential BASIC Commands

| Command      | Purpose                | Example           |
| ------------ | ---------------------- | ----------------- |
| `PRINT`      | Display text           | `PRINT "HELLO"`   |
| `INPUT`      | Get user input         | `INPUT A`         |
| `LET`        | Assign variable        | `LET A=5`         |
| `IF...THEN`  | Condition              | `IF A>5 THEN 100` |
| `GOTO`       | Jump to line           | `GOTO 10`         |
| `GOSUB`      | Call subroutine        | `GOSUB 200`       |
| `RETURN`     | Return from subroutine | `RETURN`          |
| `FOR...NEXT` | Loop                   | `FOR I=1 TO 10`   |
| `REM`        | Comment                | `REM MY PROGRAM`  |
| `END`        | Stop program           | `END`             |
| `DATA`       | Store values           | `DATA 1,2,3`      |
| `READ`       | Read DATA              | `READ A`          |
| `RESTORE`    | Reset DATA pointer     | `RESTORE`         |
| `DIM`        | Create arrays          | `DIM A(10)`       |
| `RND`        | Random numbers         | `RND(1)`          |

PC-BASIC System Commands

| Command       | Purpose                  |
| ------------- | ------------------------ |
| `RUN`         | Run program              |
| `LIST`        | Show code                |
| `NEW`         | Clear program            |
| `SAVE "NAME"` | Save program             |
| `LOAD "NAME"` | Load program             |
| `FILES`       | Show saved files         |
| `DELETE`      | Delete lines             |
| `EDIT`        | Edit line                |
| `CONT`        | Continue stopped program |

Important BASIC Functions

| Function   | Use              |
| ---------- | ---------------- |
| `INT()`    | Integer          |
| `ABS()`    | Absolute value   |
| `CHR$()`   | ASCII character  |
| `LEN()`    | String length    |
| `LEFT$()`  | Left substring   |
| `RIGHT$()` | Right substring  |
| `MID$()`   | Middle substring |

